hls: an interrupt the playlist recovered from is not its end's error

A read of a playlist's segment that the caller's interrupt callback cut
short sets the playlist AVIOContext's error to AVERROR_EXIT. Reading goes
on afterwards (an interrupt is transient), but the error stays set: when
the playlist then really ends, hls_read_packet() returns the buffer's error
in place of AVERROR_EOF, so the caller sees the old interrupt instead of
the end of the stream.

Clear AVERROR_EXIT from the buffer once the read callback returns data
again. Other errors stay as they are.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -2171,6 +2171,11 @@
     ret = read_playlist_data(opaque, buf, buf_size);
     if (ret < 0 && ret != AVERROR_EOF && ret != AVERROR_EXIT)
         v->read_error = ret;
+    /* An interrupt is transient: once data comes again, the buffer no longer
+     * carries its error, or the playlist's real end would read as that
+     * interrupt (hls_read_packet() returns the buffer's error). */
+    else if (ret > 0 && v->pb.pub.error == AVERROR_EXIT)
+        v->pb.pub.error = 0;
     return ret;
 }
 
